assumptions and how to test them
--------------------------------

T1  the output carries what the description promises: origin, step
    indices starting at 0, stale marks.
    test [ml unit]: init + 2 steps -> output contains "2 steps",
    "from", lines starting with "0" and "1"; edit step 0 (auto_replay
    off) -> "[stale]" appears on step 1.
T2  read-only honesty: no claim, repeatable, callable on a busy repl?
    — NO: the_repl on a Claimed entry errors ("is busy"). the
    description must not promise availability during operations;
    repl_list is the busy-safe overview.
    test [ml unit]: show twice -> identical; step still works.
    test [bridge]: show on A during A's slow step -> status error
    "busy" (documents the behavior; if this proves annoying in
    practice, revisit engine-side — out of scope here).
T3  full chain.
    test [e2e]: repl_show after two steps lists both.

